            <div xml:id="d156">

                <pb facs="0313" n="199" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg199"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00 R 29/2267: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Herrick</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-12-28T17:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 28,
                                1922—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6:45 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>544. B–818. Our B–816.<anchor n="31" xml:id="d156-f1"/> In final text of decision
                    given interpretation word “default” paragraph 17, annex 2, reference to
                    paragraph 18, same annex, is deleted and “default” is simply defined as
                    signifying “voluntary default.” Boyden.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herrick</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
